{"id": "section-body-17743", "title": "Oral Candidiasis", "chapterId": "chapter-sixteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "ORAL AND MAXILLOFACIAL CONDITIONS", "Fungal Infections", "Oral Candidiasis"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-17743", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Oral Candidiasis", "runs": [{"text": "Oral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Candidiasis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1126"}}, {"id": "body-17744", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "This is a fungal infection of the oral mucosa caused by Candida infection mainly Candida albicans.", "runs": [{"text": "This"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fungal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mucosa"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Candida"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mainly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Candida"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "albicans."}]}, {"id": "body-17746", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-17747", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Features of candidiasis are divided according to the types as follows:", "runs": [{"text": "Features"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "candidiasis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "divided"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "according"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "types"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "follows:"}]}, {"id": "body-17749", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Pseudomembranous", "runs": [{"text": "Pseudomembranous"}]}, {"id": "body-17750", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "White creamy patches/plaque", "runs": [{"text": "White"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "creamy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patches/plaque"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1101"}}, {"id": "body-17751", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Cover any portion of mouth but more on tongue, palate, and buccal mucosa", "runs": [{"text": "Cover"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "any"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "portion"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mouth"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "more"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tongue,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "palate,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "buccal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mucosa"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1101"}}, {"id": "body-17752", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Sometimes may present as erythematous type whereby bright erythematous mucosal lesions with only scattered white patches/plaques", "runs": [{"text": "Sometimes may present as erythematous type whereby bright erythematous mucosal lesions with only scattered"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "white patches/plaques"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1101"}}, {"id": "body-17753", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Hyperplastic", "runs": [{"text": "Hyperplastic"}]}, {"id": "body-17754", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "White patches leukoplakia-like which are not easily rubbed-off.", "runs": [{"text": "White"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patches"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leukoplakia-like"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "easily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rubbed-"}, {"text": "off."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1101"}}, {"id": "body-17756", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-17757", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Assess and correct the predisposing factor", "runs": [{"text": "Assess"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "correct"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "predisposing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "factor"}]}, {"id": "body-17759", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}]}, {"id": "body-17760", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: miconazole Oral gel 2% (PO) 2hourly", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "miconazole"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Oral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gel"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2%"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2hourly"}]}, {"id": "body-17762", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "However, in chronic mucocutaneous candidiasis with immunosuppression, topical agents may not be effective. In such instances systemic administration of fluconazole or itraconazole Is advised.", "runs": [{"text": "However, in chronic mucocutaneous candidiasis with immunosuppression, topical agents may not be effective. In such instances systemic administration of fluconazole or itraconazole Is advised."}]}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Oral and maxillofacial conditions", "start": "body-17743", "end": "body-17762"}}